From: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: h3: restore CPU PLL gating and reparenting notifiers
Date: 2026-07-28

The megous patchset removes the two safety notifiers around CPUX
frequency changes (reparent the CPU to the 24 MHz oscillator and gate
the PLL while it is being reprogrammed). Without them the cores keep
running on PLL_CPUX while it relocks, which hard-locks some boards
during the first DVFS bursts of the boot -- exactly what Armbian fixed
on sunxi-6.18 by disabling that patch (PR 10083, "fix H3/H5 RCU stall
/ CPU hang during DVFS"), a fix that never reached sunxi-6.12. The
SmartPi One freezes right after "Reached target Paths." without this.

Applied after the megous patchset, this restores the mainline
notifiers on the legacy kernel.

Signed-off-by: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun8i-h3.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun8i-h3.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun8i-h3.c
@@ -1021,8 +1021,22 @@
 
 	.resets		= sun50i_h5_ccu_resets,
 	.num_resets	= ARRAY_SIZE(sun50i_h5_ccu_resets),
+};
+
+static struct ccu_pll_nb sun8i_h3_pll_cpu_nb = {
+	.common	= &pll_cpux_clk.common,
+	/* copy from pll_cpux_clk */
+	.enable	= BIT(31),
+	.lock	= BIT(28),
 };
 
+static struct ccu_mux_nb sun8i_h3_cpu_nb = {
+	.common		= &cpux_clk.common,
+	.cm		= &cpux_clk.mux,
+	.delay_us	= 1, /* > 8 clock cycles at 24 MHz */
+	.bypass_index	= 1, /* index of 24 MHz oscillator */
+};
+
 static int sun8i_h3_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	const struct sunxi_ccu_desc *desc;
@@ -1047,6 +1061,13 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Gate then ungate PLL CPU after any rate changes */
+	ccu_pll_notifier_register(&sun8i_h3_pll_cpu_nb);
+
+	/* Reparent CPU during PLL CPU rate changes */
+	ccu_mux_notifier_register(pll_cpux_clk.common.hw.clk,
+				  &sun8i_h3_cpu_nb);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
